  "verdict": "At the r = 1/5 tuned point the light doublet has no tree-level coupling to heavy modes, so lambda_eff equals the direct H quartic, 1. The Hessian is PSD with 39 zero modes (33 broken SO(10) generators, U(1)_X, PQ and the doublet); the unbroken group is SU(3) x SU(2)_L x U(1)_T3R, not the SM, because the certified Delta_R carries hypercharge. Since the doublet is exactly flat, local minimality at tree level requires lambda_eff >= 0. If this were an SM vacuum with pure SM running below M_GUT, two-loop running would need lambda(M_GUT) = -0.0151 for the measured Higgs mass, which that condition forbids, and lambda_eff = 1 would give m_h ~ 173 GeV; neither premise holds for this benchmark. G3 stays open; nothing is excluded."
